+# Styling Daily Grind
+
+`index.html` loads `styles.css` directly; no CSS build step is required.
+
+The cascade order is declared once: `tokens`, `base`, `layout`, then
+`components`. Keep new rules inside the appropriate layer: unlayered rules
+would override all of these layers.
+
+- `tokens` defines literal palette/scale values and semantic aliases on `:root`.
+  Change semantic aliases to update the brand; use component properties such as
+  `--button-background` for local variants.
+- `base` provides page defaults and targeted, zero-specificity normalization.
+  Avoid universal resets that would affect future embedded components.
+- `layout` owns the content width and responsive grid.
+- `components` owns navigation, hero, cards, buttons, and footer. Use a class
+  as the component boundary and native nesting for related rules. Keep
+  descendant filters in `:where()` so markup structure adds no specificity.
+
+Scoping uses ordinary component classes rather than depending on `@scope`:
+there are currently no nested theme boundaries needing proximity resolution.
+Native CSS nesting and cascade layers require modern browsers. Keep token
+declarations at the top level and avoid inline presentation, IDs, `!important`,
+and deep selector chains. Prefer logical spacing and sizing properties so
+layouts also adapt to right-to-left text.
+
+Reuse the existing stock hero photograph. No runtime JavaScript or additional
+dependencies are needed for styling.
